	ZH 1:
	'I did go out for work, but I'
	R
	'didn’t get anything like that.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_03866:
	ZH 1:
	'I see...'
	R
	'That’s lame.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_037f6:
	ZH 1:
	'I’ll get you something next'
	R
	'time.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_03866:
	ZH 1:
	'Okay... Promise.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_03812:
	ZH 1:
	'Maybe Stessel’s concern isn’t'
	R
	'unreasonable...'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'Leazas is definitely putting up'
	R
	'a better fight than expected.'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'But that’s good for me.'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'The more Leazas throws this'
	R
	'country and its army into chaos,'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'the easier it is for me to take'
	R
	'action.'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'If Stessel’s that panicked,'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'a chance to take him out of his'
	R
	'position of power has to come'
	R
	'up.'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'When that happens... I’ll be'
	R
	'able to take this country for'
	R
	'myself...!'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'I went from a common soldier, to'
	R
	'a sub-captain, to a captain...'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'then to my current position of'
	R
	'general.'
	\L_0391b:
	ZH 1:
	'...Next...'
	R
	'I’ll be the empress of this'
	R
	'country.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_037f6:
	ZH 1:
	'Obedient kids lose out...'
	R
	'Act on your own ideas...'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_03866:
	ZH 1:
	'Huh?'
	R
	'What’s that?'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_037f6:
	ZH 1:
	'Nothing.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_03866:
	ZH 1:
	'Aw～... Tell me...'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_037f6:
	ZH 1:
	'Nope.'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_03866:
	ZH 1:
	'Mineva...!'
	\L_0391b:
	\L_0390e:
	\L_0382e:
	ZH 1:
	'Mineva laughed at her younger'
	R
	'brother Maha following her'
	R
	'around while they talked.'
